## Root Cause
The use of unserialize directly on user-controlled input without validation can lead to deserialization vulnerabilities, enabling attackers to craft malicious input.

## Explanation
The patch replaces the unsafe unserialize function with a safe deserialization library that validates and sanitizes the input before parsing. This ensures that any potentially harmful data is rejected, mitigating the risk of exploitation.

